{"retractions" [[17592186344222 :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{x}^{x+y}(y+2z)\\,dz]dA & ={∬}_{D}[yz+{z}^{2}]_{z=x}^{z=x+y}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y((x+y)-x)+((x+y)^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}+2xy+{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}2xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}2xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[x{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x({x}^{2}-0)+\\frac{2}{3}({x}^{3}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{3}\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}(16-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186344224 17592186344225 17592186344226 17592186344227 17592186344228] "immutable_fields" [[17592186344223 :answer-field/id] [17592186344223 :answer-field/key] [17592186344223 :answer-field/type] [17592186344223 :answer-field/correct] [17592186344223 :answer-field/choices]]}
